\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1.  Come unto me Christ Jesus says
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 You heavy laden and labour,
\par all you adults and children
\par Yet all men and yet all women\tab 
\par I'll give you everlasting rest
\par and heal you from all illness.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  For my burden is so weightless
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 who ever takes and follow me,
\par shall have life everlasting.
\par I will give to him my guidance,
\par deliver him and take him to
\par my Kingdom in the heavens
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. People on earth do dwell for peace,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 but many troubles of Christians,
\par make them so weak and frightened;
\par but that is the only one way
\par that all our troubles and weary
\par shall come to pass and over.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  All creatures of the whole wild world
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Those from the sea and from the earth
\par And those from the sky tells us
\par that worry and weariness
\par awaits us so we must be strong
\par that we may not be conquered.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.  A man can be so strong today
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Tomorrow he will be no more
\par  that is the will of Christ Lord
\par  things on this earth will go so bad
\par  like flowers blossomed on the plains
\par and weather off and perish.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  6.  Sinners are so afraid of death
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj   and even on the bed of death,
\par   they seemed to seek repentance;
\par   the sons of men do what please them
\par   and so their souls are very poor
\par   and set their eyes on things here.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  7. Knowledge is un-knowledgeable
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 and in vain shall their glory be
\par and all shall pass away soon.
\par If one accepts the word of God
\par in this opportune time of grace,
\par he shall for ever be saved.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  8.  And what the Lord has promised us
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 thro' His own words to every man
\par His covenant will so dwell
\par And He will fulfil His promise
\par and save us in the name of Christ,
\par \pard       take us to Heaven! Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

